       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Acetaminophen 2000 mg three times daily comes to 6,000 mg/day. That's well above the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day (often 3,000 mg/day in practice). A single 2,000 mg dose is also double the typical maximum single dose of 1,000 mg. At this dose, the risk of hepatotoxicity is serious, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you do want 2000 mg three times daily, tell me and add a note with the clinical rationale. I can enter it with that note, but I'd like your explicit confirmation first. Otherwise, tell me which regimen to enter."
      }
